    {
      "id": "45bdc31b0d2d706465f8420cb86f43c6822d1aa2",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 490169042,
          "type": null,
          "body": "@chuckcraft: Sure, if an approach can be agreed upon I'd be willing to do the needful to update the other installers.\n\n@crondaemon: The issue isn't specific to developers. I'm not wanting to develop an `extcap` but run an existing one.\n\n@graham.bloice: The existing *extcap.html* documentation on review could use some work:\n\n> WINDOWS USER: Because of restrictions directly calling the script may not always work. In such a case, a batch file may be provided, which then in turn executes the script. Please refer to doc/extcap_example.py for more information.\n\nThe referenced `extcap_example.py` doesn't exist on Windows (I haven't checked Linux/macOS). Nor does the `doc` directory.\n\n> When Wireshark launches an extcap, it automatically adds its installation path (c:\\Program Files\\Wireshark\\) to the DLL search path so that the extcap library dependencies can be found (it is not designed to be launched by hand).\n\nThis is accurate but only implies the solution rather than telling users explicitly what needs to be done to execute these utilities directly.\n\nAbove suggestions aside, a HTML file can't be easily viewed in a terminal, which to my mind makes it less suitable than a simple plain text *README* which can be trivially viewed in the same environment as the programs being executed.\n\nIt sounds like there's a fair amount of resistance to adding the proposed additional documentation, and I'm not overly invested in progressing this change. It was only intended to help other Wireshark users who I expect will encounter the same problems I did which were non-obvious to me how to resolve. If there's no agreed path forward I'm content to close this MR and associated issue and it can be revisited in future if desired.",
          "author": {
            "id": 51592,
            "username": "ralish",
            "public_email": "sdl@nexiom.net",
            "name": "Samuel D. Leslie",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/587b20ae2b09503e2e109859632704d87a7f458e61051bfb295083166bebc3f7?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/ralish"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-01-20T20:42:52.226Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-01-20T20:42:52.226Z",
